From: Gustavo Morinaga <me@gustavomorinaga.dev>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 02:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] cellPad: on Windows the poll gate's clock is the performance
 counter

pad_now_ms was GetTickCount64 on Windows, which moves in 15.6 ms steps
(the system timer; timeBeginPeriod does not change it). The 4 ms poll
gate then let one host poll through a step: pads, keyboard and mouse were
read at 64 Hz, not up to 250. Above 64 fps the mouse's counts came on
some frames in lumps and on the frames between not at all, so at 144 fps
a view turned by the mouse, and the gun swaying with it, moved in steps;
sticks and buttons were as late. QueryPerformanceCounter in ms instead,
as CLOCK_MONOTONIC off Windows (unchanged).
---
 libs/input/cellPad.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -1060,10 +1060,22 @@
     }
     return f;
 }
+/* Milliseconds on a monotonic clock, for the poll gate and the pad's timers.
+ * On Windows from the performance counter: GetTickCount64 moves in steps of
+ * the system timer, 15.6 ms (timeBeginPeriod does not change it), so the
+ * PAD_POLL_INTERVAL_MS gate let one poll through a step: the host was read at
+ * 64 Hz, not 250. Above 64 fps the mouse's counts then came on some frames in
+ * lumps and on the frames between not at all (at 144 fps a view that turns,
+ * and a gun that sways, in steps), and pads' sticks and buttons were as late. */
 static unsigned long long pad_now_ms(void)
 {
 #ifdef _WIN32
-    return (unsigned long long)GetTickCount64();
+    static LARGE_INTEGER f;   /* set once; every thread stores the same value */
+    LARGE_INTEGER c;
+    if (!f.QuadPart) QueryPerformanceFrequency(&f);
+    QueryPerformanceCounter(&c);
+    const unsigned long long q = (unsigned long long)c.QuadPart, hz = (unsigned long long)f.QuadPart;
+    return q / hz * 1000ull + q % hz * 1000ull / hz;
 #else
     struct timespec ts;
     clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
